    path: "essays/repetition-feels-like-truth.html", image: "/assets/visuals/repetition-truth-check.svg",
    title: "Repetition Can Feel Like Truth—even When You Know Better",
    metaTitle: "Why Repetition Feels True | Life in the Simulation",
    description: "Why repeated claims become easier to believe, what illusory-truth research actually shows, and how to interrupt familiarity before it becomes evidence.",
    dek: "A claim can acquire the texture of truth without acquiring new evidence. Repetition makes language easier to process, easier to retrieve and harder to recognize as merely familiar.",
